# Template only. A real frontend/.env.production is NOT needed for the Docker build
# and should generally not exist — frontend/.dockerignore excludes .env* from the
# build context so a stray copy can't become a misleading second source of truth.
#
# The production value is passed as a build-arg instead:
#   docker compose -f docker-compose.prod.yaml build \
#     --build-arg NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://putyouon.app frontend
#
# The frontend Dockerfile fails the build if that arg is empty rather than shipping
# an image whose API calls silently hit the frontend's own origin.
#
# Keep this file as the record of which variable production needs. Copy it to
# .env.production only if you are running `next build`/`next start` on a host
# directly, outside Docker.

NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://putyouon.app
